The requested Python function needs to group song titles by their first letter case-insensitively, maintain the order of keys based on their first appearance in the input, and ensure the internal lists of titles are sorted alphabetically. The initial provided solution correctly handles grouping and sorting, but the requirement specifies that the keys must follow the order of their first appearance. Since Python 3.7+, dictionaries maintain insertion order, iterating through the list once and appending to the dictionary keys as they are encountered naturally satisfies this condition. The provided code logic matches these requirements.

